<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.00 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.00 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0750 to the dollar, up from 3.0875 on Wednesday and at 1.8300 to the mark, down from 1.8250, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The NBP fixed the zloty at an average of 3.00 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Wednesday's 2.93 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
